.TH ORBITVIEWTEST 1
.SH NAME
orbitviewtest \- test that draworbits() keeps the focus body pinned at view centre
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B orbitviewtest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Orbitviewtest
calls
.IR danby-aerobraking (1)'s
own in-process
.B viewtest()
seam \(em a test-only entry point, the same justification
.BR run() 's
own comment gives for existing at all (see
.IR eqnorbitaltest (1)).
.B Viewtest
drives the model forward through
.BR viewgeometry() ,
the exact function
.B draworbits()
itself calls to decide where the most massive body (\*(lqthe
planet\*(rq) lands on screen and how far zoomed in the view is \(em
not a second copy of that logic that could silently drift from the
real one.
.PP
At three different view rectangle sizes, every step of a full run (or
a generous cap, whichever comes first) is checked for:
.TP
.B focus
the index of the body with the largest mass \(em checked against the
model's own mass values directly, not assumed.
.TP
.B centre
exactly the given view rectangle's own geometric midpoint \(em checked
against an independently computed midpoint, not
.BR viewgeometry() 's
own formula recomputed a second time.
.TP
.B scale
strictly positive throughout, and different at least once across the
run. A
.B scale
that never changes would mean the zoom half of the fix silently
stopped happening \(em found this exact way once already, while first
writing this test: an initial 300-step run never showed the orbit
decay enough for
.B scale
to move at all, which turned out to be nothing wrong with
.BR viewgeometry() ,
just too short a run for a 0.0025-step, 30.0-\c
.B maxtime
model (see BUGS).
.PP
Exits with
.B PASS
if every check held at every step and every view size, or
.B FAIL
naming what failed, at which step, and at which view size.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/orbitviewtest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-aerobraking (1),
.IR eqnorbitaltest (1)
.SH BUGS
The step cap (15000, covering the model's own full 30.0/0.0025 run)
is specific to this one model's own timing; a test built the same way
against a different Orbital-family model driven through
.IR appl/lib/danbylab.b
would need its own cap sized the same way \(em checked against that
model's own
.BR maxtime / step ,
not assumed from this one.
